# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# CONFIDENTIAL — never commit to this public repo
# Real EvoEnergy network models and customer/NMI data, and anything derived
# from them. If you add new real-data files, extend these patterns.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# Raw CIM/DMS network exports (network topology + customer UsagePoints/NMIs)
*.xml

# Converted network models built from real exports (topology + placed NMIs)
*_network.json
*_network*.json
*_lv_network.json
GOLDCR_*.json
LEXCEN_*.json
S5402*.json
S_*_AT*.json
S_*_lv*.json
network_conversion/*.json
*.parquet
*.npz

# Synthetic profiles for unmapped NMIs. These are REAL metered profiles copied
# onto other NMI ids, and the report contains a real-NMI -> real-NMI donor map,
# so they are exactly as confidential as the raw meter data.
examples/scenario_real/
**/background_timeseries.csv
**/disaggregation_report.json
**/synthetic_report.json

# Real interval-meter / NMI data and anything derived from it
examples/scenario_2/
examples/scenario_2/data_translation/lexcen_data.csv
examples/scenario_2/data_translation/project_format.csv
examples/scenario_2/forecast_timeseries.csv
examples/scenario_2/network.json

# All pipeline inputs (real meter/NMI data, XMLs, mappings, ambient caches).
# The folder structure itself is documented via the committed READMEs.
data/
!data/**/README.md

# Derived, regenerable
build/

# Results (rows keyed by nmi_<NMI>) and old run outputs
out/
results/
**/curtailment_report.csv
**/feeder_summary.csv

# Archived originals (old generated outputs from real data live here)
archive/

# Local run guide that references real feeder/substation names — keep private
# (both the pre-reorg and post-reorg locations)
examples/RUN_DOE_GUIDE.md
examples/legacy/RUN_DOE_GUIDE.md

# Orchestration and reporting that name real feeders and substations. Same
# reasoning as RUN_DOE_GUIDE.md above: the generic library code is public,
# anything carrying the DNSP's network identifiers is not.
scripts/run_all_feeders.py
docs/RUN_ALL_FEEDERS.md
tools/make_paper_figures.py
tools/plot_utilisation_vs_benefit.py
run_*.sh
run_*.log
COMMIT_PLAN.md

# Paper figures and tables. Labelled with real feeder names and derived from
# the confidential runs; the manuscript itself lives outside this repo.
paper/
